\contentsline {todo}{\fcolorbox {black}{red!25}{\textcolor {red!25}{o}}\ \textbf {MD suggestion:} Potresti scrivere "An air- or gas-filled hollow core, where $n_{\text {core}} \approx 1 < n_{\text {clad}} \approx 1.45$, cannot guide light by TIR because the required refractive index contrast is inverted. Nevertheless, such a core enables light propagation through a medium that is significantly less dispersive, nonlinear, and absorptive than silica, while also granting optical access to atoms, molecules, and particles that a solid core excludes. The central challenge of hollow-core fiber (HCF) technology is therefore to achieve optical confinement without relying on conventional index guiding."}{6}{section*.11}%
